    "status": "present",
    "value": "Merge exactly k consecutive stone piles at each step, paying their total weight, to reach one pile at minimum cost; return minus one if impossible. The approach is: interval DP maintains the reducible pile-count residue; split only at compatible boundaries. Its target cost is O(n^3/(k-1)) time/O(n^2) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
